to each row.\n\nNormalized values still appear, but only in the `_normalized` columns.\n\n**SIS v2 stays the raw-observation contract.** It still serves raw observations, not reported values. The only change is two new nullable fields on each observation, `attemptId` and `batchId`, declared in the v2 capabilities. Source observations, cursors and counts are unchanged.\n\n**Out of scope here:** the report's own basis, rounding and revision numbering stay as #211 and #212 shipped them. This PR changes only what the exports read; it does not touch how reports are built. The stored-unit, censoring and ambiguity guards from f830 are kept as they are.\n\nHow: `reportedValueReadService` now returns per-value batch ids. The export controllers and `sisAdapterService` read from it instead of from raw results. `issue_213_export_equals_report.test.js` checks that the export equals the report for each path. The help release manifest is regenerated for the three new translation keys.\n\nChecks at 990a4cb5, rebased on main f830f900:\n- `issue_213_export_equals_report`, `export_normalization` and `sis_adapter_service` pass, 27 of 27 tests.\n- The 17 server suites that touch the changed files pass, 247 of 247 tests.\n- Client build passes, and lint shows 0 errors and 14 warnings.\n- The full server suite is running on this head.\n\nRefs #213. The audit-gate convention is that #213 closes only after the post-deploy check, so this PR deliberately says Refs rather than Closes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01869phMNBbSrZkcCR7UBe9J","created_at":"2026-10-12T02:57:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T03:39:21Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9f557d9b427e59876a524f45c3fc124c8d700d15","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yigini/soilfer-lims/pulls/293/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.gi